Fixed: Treat user-specified coefficients as zero or one only if they are exactly zero or one in IBAMR::IBRedundantInitializer (boundary mass), IBAMR::IBStandardInitializer (stiffness warnings), IBAMR::IBFEMethod (Phi_epsilon), IBAMR::INSCollocatedHierarchyIntegrator (density), and the variable-coefficient staggered Navier-Stokes integrators (damping coefficient, condition number scaling). IBAMR::INSCollocatedHierarchyIntegrator also no longer changes the scaling of its projection if the time-step size is smaller than about 1.5e-8.
<br>
(Boyce Griffith, 2026/10/05)
